### What does this question ask?

The interviewer wants you to filter a stream using a negated membership check against a collection of values. This tests your understanding of `Set.contains`, negation in predicates, and the performance difference between Set and List for lookups.

### How do you filter employees not in a set of departments?

```java
package com.bank.hr;

import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class ExcludeDepartments {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Employee> employees = Employee.getSampleEmployees();

        Set<String> excluded = Set.of("IT", "HR");

        List<Employee> result = employees.stream()
            .filter(e -> !excluded.contains(e.getDepartment()))
            .toList();

        result.forEach(e ->
            System.out.println(e.getName() + " - " + e.getDepartment()));
    }
}
```

